3. 養聲

廣東話：你把聲沙晒，呢幾日都係講少啲嘢養下聲啦。
English: Your voice is super hoarse, you should talk less these few days to rest your vocal cords.

4. 票尾

廣東話：記住入閘之後唔好咁快掉咗張飛，留返個票尾喺度做收據啊。
English: Remember not to throw away the ticket too quickly after entering the gate, keep the ticket stub as a receipt.

5. hacker

廣東話：聽講嗰間大公司嘅系統俾hacker入侵咗，好多客資料都外洩添。
English: I heard that big company's system was hacked by a hacker, and a lot of customer data was leaked.

6. 石斛蘭

廣東話：石斛蘭同其他蘭花唔同，佢鍾意依附喺樹幹上面生長，唔使種落泥度。
English: Dendrobium is different from other orchids; it likes to grow attached to tree trunks and doesn't need to be planted in soil.

7. 吊詭

廣東話：呢個邏輯問題好吊詭，你愈諗只會愈覺得矛盾。
English: This logic problem is very paradoxical; the more you think about it, the more contradictory it feels.

8. 吊詭

廣東話：佢明明做緊犯法嘅嘢，仲可以義正辭嚴咁鬧人，真係好吊詭。
English: He is clearly doing something illegal, yet he can righteously scold others; it's truly absurd.

9. 各為其主

廣東話：商場如戰場，大家各為其主，就算以前係好朋友，而家喺談判桌上都係對手。
English: Business is like a battlefield; everyone acts for their own boss. Even if they were good friends before, they are opponents at the negotiating table now.

10. 軨蓋

廣東話：你架車個軨蓋刮花咗，要攞去車房噴過油先得。
English: The hubcap of your car is scratched; you need to take it to the garage to get it repainted.

11. 打哥夫

廣東話：聽日天氣咁好，不如我哋去打哥夫鬆下筋骨啦。
English: The weather is so nice tomorrow, why don't we go play golf to stretch our muscles?

12. 免揀

廣東話：街市嗰檔生果檔寫住「免揀」，你只可以由老闆幫你執，唔畀自己揀㗎。
English: The fruit stall at the market says "no picking"; you can only let the boss pack it for you, you aren't allowed to pick it yourself.

13. 擺闊佬

廣東話：佢次次出親街都買晒名牌，真係鍾意擺闊佬。
English: Every time he goes out, he buys only designer brands; he really likes to show off his wealth.

14. 廣播劇

廣東話：以前未有電視嗰陣，啲人最鍾意收音機聽廣播劇嚟解悶。
English: Before there were TVs, people loved listening to radio dramas on the radio to relieve boredom.

15. 錄影機

廣東話：我想錄低今晚嗰套劇集，唔知部錄影機壞咗未呢？
English: I want to record that TV series tonight, I wonder if the video recorder is broken?

16. 吟詩吟唔甩

廣東話：人哋都已經有閉路電視拍低晒成個過程，你重喺度拗，吟詩吟唔甩㗎啦。
English: They already have CCTV footage of the whole process, and you're still arguing; with solid evidence, you can't talk your way out of it.

17. 佈道大會

廣東話：教會今個禮拜日會喺大球場搞個大型嘅佈道大會，你有冇興趣去睇下？
English: The church will hold a large-scale evangelistic rally at the stadium this Sunday, are you interested in going to see it?

18. 寫手

廣東話：佢係一個全職寫手，每日都要寫幾千字交畀編輯。
English: He is a full-time writer who has to write several thousand words every day to hand in to the editor.

19. 寫手

廣東話：個政客搵咗個槍手做寫手，幫佢代筆出回憶錄。
English: The politician hired a ghostwriter to write his memoirs on his behalf.

20. 代打

廣東話：我今晚要OT，可唔可以幫我代打呢個online game嘅日常任務啊？
English: I have to work overtime tonight, can you help me do the daily quests in this online game on my behalf?

21. 茶碗

廣東話：佢好鍾意日本茶道，特登去京都買咗幾隻靚陶瓷茶碗返嚟。
English: He really likes the Japanese tea ceremony and specifically went to Kyoto to buy a few beautiful ceramic tea bowls.

22. 茶隔

廣東話：你沖茶嗰陣記得用個茶隔隔走啲茶葉，唔係飲親就麻煩啦。
English: Remember to use a tea strainer to separate the tea leaves when brewing tea, otherwise it will be troublesome if you choke on them while drinking.

23. 只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈

廣東話：老闆自己遲到就話開會，我哋遲到一分鐘就扣人工，真係只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈！
English: The boss says it's just a meeting when he is late, but if we are one minute late, our salary gets deducted; it's truly a double standard where those in power can do whatever they want while ordinary people are restricted!

24. 獨唱

廣東話：今晚個晚會，佢會有一段五分鐘嘅獨唱表演。
English: At tonight's gala, she will have a five-minute solo performance.

25. 快人快事

廣東話：同佢傾生意真係快人快事，十分鐘就傾掂晒所有細節。
English: Doing business with him is really a case of a straightforward person doing things quickly; all the details were settled in ten minutes.

26. 四腳獸

廣東話：聽講商場男廁又有四腳獸喺入面搞嘢，真係離譜。
English: I heard there were "four-legged beasts" doing things inside the men's restroom at the mall again, it's truly outrageous.

27. 無米粥

廣東話：大家而家只係傾緊個初步計劃，仲有好多細節未落實，都只係煲緊無米粥啫。
English: We are only discussing a preliminary plan right now, and many details are not yet finalized; it's just an initial talk without concrete commitments.

28. 義會

廣東話：以前基層市民好難喺銀行借錢，有急需嗰陣就唯有靠朋友搞義會去籌筆錢。
English: In the past, it was hard for grassroots citizens to borrow money from banks; when in urgent need, they could only rely on friends to organize a mutual aid society to raise funds.

29. 榜文

廣東話：縣衙門出面貼咗張榜文，懸紅緝拿嗰個通緝犯。
English: A notice was posted outside the county magistrate's office, offering a reward for the capture of the wanted criminal.

30. MK名

廣東話：而家啲後生仔上網改個名都好鍾意加埋一堆特殊符號，真係好有以前嗰種MK名嘅風格。
English: Nowadays, when young people name themselves online, they like to add a bunch of special symbols; it really has the style of those old "MK names". [end of text]


